# Service Definition — hcv (Housing Compliance Vault)

## Product

Housing Compliance Vault (HCV) — supplier qualification evidence management for UK housing compliance, built on the chapelgate/business-evidence-wallet repository (Housing Compliance Vault per README.md). Multi-tenant evidence vault that lets organisations upload evidence documents (PDF, DOCX, XLSX, TXT), extract candidate facts, have humans approve them with provenance, and generate compliance/evidence packs. Used by suppliers and buyers who need to evidence qualifications, insurance, certificates, contracts, housing compliance and construction certifications (CSCS, CPCS, SMAS).

## Lot

Cloud Software (SaaS)

## Description

Multi-tenant evidence wallet that lets organisations upload evidence documents (PDF, DOCX, XLSX, TXT), extract candidate facts, have humans approve them with provenance, and generate compliance/evidence packs. Organisations can prove what they claim. Used by suppliers and buyers who need to evidence qualifications, insurance, certificates, contracts and housing compliance certifications.

## Key features

- Organisations, roles, invitations (capability codes, not email-identity join)
- Evidence upload (PDF, DOCX, XLSX, TXT) with safe text extraction; file validation accepts text files and rejects empty, oversize, executable files, double-extension executables and PDF magic with non-PDF extension
- Candidate fact extraction (heuristic always; optional AI) — extracts PL limit and expiry from labelled certificates, EL at £5m, employees, turnover, ISO; caps questionnaire questions so a huge file cannot amplify inserts
- Human review with provenance and fact versions
- Candidate correction before approval (original extraction kept; OCC on concurrent edits); normalises public liability limit from typed correction; rejects empty, injection and non-money limit edits
- Expiry, conflicts, dependency reevaluation; conflict engine flags disagreeing live values (PL £5m vs £10m) without picking a winner; ignores archived facts
- Questionnaire ingest and evidence-backed response packs; parses PAS 91, SSIP, CHAS, Constructionline templates without fabricating questions; includes all UK construction templates
- GREEN/AMBER/RED/EXPIRED/CONFLICT status (never silently upgraded); fail-closed wording — RED/EXPIRED/CONFLICT wording never confirms the requirement is met
- JSON/XLSX/DOCX export, reopened and verified; export integrity round-trips JSON and rejects GREEN without facts; strips XML 1.0 forbidden control characters before escaping; rejects oversized export fields before OOXML generation; spreadsheet formula neutralization prefixes formula-like cells so they stay literal text
- Audit trail; invalidation marks dependent answers when a fact is superseded

## Intended users

Public sector buyers and suppliers who need to evidence qualifications, insurance, certificates, case facts and housing compliance certifications.

## Data handled

Untrusted document text sliced to 12,000 chars and wrapped via wrapUntrusted before optional AI model call. No PII intentionally added; input may contain user document content. Output claims validated against ClaimListSchema (max 40 claims, bounded fields). Personal data may be present in uploaded documents.

## AI/ML use

Optional AI grok-4.5 for candidate fact extraction. Output is candidate-only; human must approve. Fail-closed: if model unavailable or output fails schema validation, no claims persisted. Deterministic threshold engine gates evidence status; no model may override. Prompt safety corpus lock: wraps untrusted text and detects injection corpus.

